+    <h2>1. Overview of Privacy by Design &amp; Data Minimization</h2>
+    <p><strong>General Information</strong></p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is built following <strong>Privacy by Design</strong>, <strong>Data Minimization</strong>, and <strong>User Transparency</strong> principles. By default, non-essential third-party scripts (such as analytics and advertising networks) are disabled unless you explicitly opt in via our Privacy Preferences control. We also honor browser-level privacy signals including <em>Global Privacy Control (GPC)</em> and <em>Do Not Track (DNT)</em>.</p>
+
+    <h2>2. Data Collection &amp; Purpose Limitation</h2>
+    <p><strong>Account Registration and Authentication (Sign Up &amp; Sign In)</strong></p>
+    <p>When you create an account or sign in, we collect only the minimum data strictly necessary for authentication:</p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Username:</strong> A pseudonymous identifier chosen by you. We encourage using a handle rather than your real name or email address.</li>
+        <li><strong>Password:</strong> Used solely to verify your identity during authentication.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p>Authentication requests are sent with <code>referrerPolicy: "no-referrer"</code>, omitted third-party credentials, and are explicitly excluded from analytics tracking (<code>data-skip-tracking="true"</code>). Passwords are never stored in browser storage, and authentication tokens are not persisted in insecure local storage.</p>
+
+    <h2>3. Cookies, Local Storage, and Session Data</h2>
+    <p><strong>Strictly Necessary Data</strong></p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Reading List Session:</strong> We do not initialize session cookies merely for visiting the website. A server session is only populated when you actively bookmark an article for your Reading List.</li>
+        <li><strong>Privacy Consent Preferences:</strong> Your opt-in/opt-out choices for analytics and advertising are stored locally in your browser under <code>devtools_times_privacy_consent</code> so we can respect your choices across page loads.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>4. Third-Party Scripts &amp; External Resources</h2>
+    <p><strong>Opt-In Analytics &amp; Advertising</strong></p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Analytics (<code>analytics-client.js</code>):</strong> Disabled by default. Only loaded if you explicitly opt in to Analytics in Privacy Preferences (and when DNT/GPC is not enabled).</li>
+        <li><strong>Advertising (<code>ad-client.js</code> &amp; Ad Slots):</strong> Disabled by default. Ad network scripts and ad slot registrations only run if you explicitly opt in to Third-Party Advertising.</li>
+        <li><strong>Web Fonts:</strong> Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts using strict referrer and Content Security Policy rules.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>5. Document Security &amp; Privacy Headers</h2>
+    <p>To protect your browsing privacy and prevent unauthorized cross-site tracking or data leakage, all responses include strict HTTP headers:</p>
